/*  liquidDiffusivity02 -- the multicomponent liquid diffusivity of Kooijman &
    Taylor (1991), on their own Table I (DEV.md 4c C329, slice B2a).

    WHAT IT SHOWS.  Acetone (1) / benzene (2) / carbon tetrachloride (3) at
    25 C.  At each of the paper's four compositions (and at a fifth, the one
    of Taylor & Krishna 1993, Example 4.2.6, p. 92) the operation prints
        D_L_MS_<i>_<j>      the three Maxwell-Stefan pair values in the mixture,
                            Eq. 23 of the paper (D0_ij^xj D0_ji^xi times
                            (D0_ik D0_jk)^(xk/2) for the third component);
        Gamma_<i>_<j>       the thermodynamic-factor matrix of the NRTL liquid
                            (paper Eq. 4: a central difference of ln gamma, step
                            1e-6 in mole fraction, component 3 -- the LAST --
                            taking the change);
        D_L_Fick_<i>_<j>   the Fick matrix [B]^-1 [Gamma] (paper Eqs. 6-8), in
                            1e-9 m2/s a student reads against the measured one
                            below.  It depends on which component is numbered
                            last, and carbon tetrachloride is, as in the paper;
        D_L_effective_<c>   the effective diffusivity of each component by
                            Wilke's reduction (Taylor & Krishna 1993, Eq.
                            6.1.14): what a rate-based column's film would take.

    THE MEASURED MATRIX (the paper's Table I, molar-average frame, 1e-9 m2/s,
    D11 D12 D21 D22; Cullinan & Toor 1965, converted by the authors):
        x = 0.2989 0.3490 0.3521   1.8690 -0.2129 -0.0043 2.2730
        x = 0.1496 0.1499 0.7005   1.5968 -0.0592 -0.0771 1.8132
        x = 0.1497 0.6984 0.1519   1.9652  0.0137 -0.1522 1.9248
        x = 0.6999 0.1497 0.1504   2.3041 -0.4019  0.1848 2.9969
    THE ACCEPTANCE (gate check_liquid_diffusivity_declaration, arm 5b): the
    average of the paper's discrepancy |D_calc - D_expt| / D_ii over the four
    points within 1e-4 of the paper's Table IV, column "eq 23" (overall
    0.0763, diagonal 0.0916, off-diagonal 0.0611); Gamma at 0.70/0.15/0.15
    to Taylor & Krishna's printed matrix, every digit, [0.788 -0.088; 0.075
    1.043] (tau_21 = 0.76432 as Taylor & Krishna print it; the paper's Table I prints
    0.74632, and with that the numbers are 0.002 away: the thermophysical dict says so).  Nothing is fitted: the six D0 and the NRTL parameters are the
    sources' inputs.

    WHAT IT DOES NOT SHOW.  Nothing about an associating liquid: the paper's own
    Table IV gives 0.19 on acetone / benzene / methanol, with a maximum of 0.71,
    and says why (the Vignes equation does not perform well for associating
    binaries).  The rule is an interpolation of six numbers, not a theory.

    THE MISPRINT.  The two books print the limiting value of the third
    component as (D0_ik D0_ki)^(1/2) (Taylor & Kooijman 2014, Eq. 3.41; Taylor
    & Krishna 1993, Eq. 4.2.19); the paper's Eq. 21 is (D0_ik D0_jk)^(1/2),
    and it is the one implemented.  On this table the paper's form scores
    0.078 and the books' 0.100 (each pair evaluated for i < j and copied; the
    books' form is not symmetric, so the number depends on that order) (Theory Guide, section "The multicomponent
    liquid diffusivity", prints the measurement).

    The golden master locks every computed value at reltol 1e-4.  */

operations
(
    {
        name        t1;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { acetone 0.2989;  benzene 0.349;  carbonTetrachloride 0.3521; } }
        properties  ( D_L_MS_acetone_benzene D_L_MS_acetone_carbonTetrachloride D_L_MS_benzene_carbonTetrachloride
                      Gamma_acetone_acetone Gamma_acetone_benzene Gamma_benzene_acetone Gamma_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_Fick_acetone_acetone D_L_Fick_acetone_benzene D_L_Fick_benzene_acetone D_L_Fick_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_effective_acetone D_L_effective_benzene D_L_effective_carbonTetrachloride );
    }
    {
        name        t2;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { acetone 0.1496;  benzene 0.1499;  carbonTetrachloride 0.7005; } }
        properties  ( D_L_MS_acetone_benzene D_L_MS_acetone_carbonTetrachloride D_L_MS_benzene_carbonTetrachloride
                      Gamma_acetone_acetone Gamma_acetone_benzene Gamma_benzene_acetone Gamma_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_Fick_acetone_acetone D_L_Fick_acetone_benzene D_L_Fick_benzene_acetone D_L_Fick_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_effective_acetone D_L_effective_benzene D_L_effective_carbonTetrachloride );
    }
    {
        name        t3;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { acetone 0.1497;  benzene 0.6984;  carbonTetrachloride 0.1519; } }
        properties  ( D_L_MS_acetone_benzene D_L_MS_acetone_carbonTetrachloride D_L_MS_benzene_carbonTetrachloride
                      Gamma_acetone_acetone Gamma_acetone_benzene Gamma_benzene_acetone Gamma_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_Fick_acetone_acetone D_L_Fick_acetone_benzene D_L_Fick_benzene_acetone D_L_Fick_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_effective_acetone D_L_effective_benzene D_L_effective_carbonTetrachloride );
    }
    {
        name        t4;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { acetone 0.6999;  benzene 0.1497;  carbonTetrachloride 0.1504; } }
        properties  ( D_L_MS_acetone_benzene D_L_MS_acetone_carbonTetrachloride D_L_MS_benzene_carbonTetrachloride
                      Gamma_acetone_acetone Gamma_acetone_benzene Gamma_benzene_acetone Gamma_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_Fick_acetone_acetone D_L_Fick_acetone_benzene D_L_Fick_benzene_acetone D_L_Fick_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_effective_acetone D_L_effective_benzene D_L_effective_carbonTetrachloride );
    }
    {
        name        tk93;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 298.15 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { acetone 0.7;  benzene 0.15;  carbonTetrachloride 0.15; } }
        properties  ( D_L_MS_acetone_benzene D_L_MS_acetone_carbonTetrachloride D_L_MS_benzene_carbonTetrachloride
                      Gamma_acetone_acetone Gamma_acetone_benzene Gamma_benzene_acetone Gamma_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_Fick_acetone_acetone D_L_Fick_acetone_benzene D_L_Fick_benzene_acetone D_L_Fick_benzene_benzene
                      D_L_effective_acetone D_L_effective_benzene D_L_effective_carbonTetrachloride );
    }
);
